<div>
  <title>Lesson Activities</title>
  <para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
</div>
<list>
  <item>2.15.1: Analyzing Graphs that Represent Linear Equations and Inequalities</item>
  <item>2.15.2: Determining if Points on Boundary Lines Are Solutions to a System</item>
  <list>
  <item>2.15.2: Self Check</item>
  <item>2.15.2: Additional Resources</item></list>
  <item>2.15.3: Solving Problems to Satisfy Multiple Constraints Simultaneously</item><list>
  <item>2.15.3: Self Check</item>
  <item>2.15.3: Additional Resources</item></list>
  <item>2.15.4: Identifying Graph Regions Included in a System’s Solution</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 2.15.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<div>
  <para>Pre-printed slips, cut from copies of the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8d4c4466af059347e91085c2bbe84c8c4031254c">blackline master of data and problem cards</link>Coordinate Grids</para>
</div>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<div>
  <list>
    <item>None</item>
  </list>
</div>
<div>
  <title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
  <para>During this lesson, it is
    important to:</para>
</div>
<div>
  <list>
    <item>Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see
      throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for these words and notice
      their use and meanings.</item>
    <item>Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and
        their written and oral explanations.</item>
    <item>Utilize a word wall. Sample cards
      are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link></item>
  </list>
  <!--[if !supportLists]-->
</div>
<div>
  <para>Vocabulary words that are
      emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
 </div>
